# ── Firebase (impala-android-demo) ────────────────────────────
impala-android-demo/app/google-services.json

# ── Vendored JavaCard kits: committed in full (KEEP THIS LAST) ─
# impala-card/applet/libs/sdks/ holds the Oracle kits the CAP build converts with. Their export
# files (*.exp, *.jca) and sample keystores match the build-output patterns above, but there they
# are inputs: without them the converter fails ("export file lang.exp of package java.lang not
# found"). A negation only wins when it comes after the pattern it overrides, so this block stays at
# the end of the file. Without it, adding or updating a kit (the JDK 21 plan vendors
# jc320v26.0_kit) would leave those files out of the commit without a word, and the CAP would stop
# converting in CI and in every other checkout. The kits' own .gitignore still drops .DS_Store.
!impala-card/applet/libs/sdks/**
